{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2220,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  If you have polarized sunglasses,\nyou have a quantum measurement device."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5920,
    "dDurationMs": 3719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Each of these pieces of glass is what's\ncalled a \"polarizing filter\", which means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9639,
    "dDurationMs": 4161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when a photon of light reaches the glass,\nit either passes through, or it doesn’t."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13800,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And whether or not it passes through is effectively\na measurement of whether that photon is polarized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18880,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a given direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19880,
    "dDurationMs": 3869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  Try this: Find yourself several sets\nof polarized sunglasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23749,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look through one set of sunglasses at some\nlight source, like a lamp, then hold a second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28439,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polarizing filter, between you and the light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30529,
    "dDurationMs": 3501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you rotate that second filter, the lamp\nwill look lighter and darker."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34030,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It should look darkest when the second filter\nis oriented 90 degrees off from the first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38300,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you're observing is that the photons\nwith polarization that allows them to pass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41320,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a filter along one axis have a much\nlower probability of passing through a second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44990,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "filter along a perpendicular axis – in principle\n0%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48350,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Here's where things get quantum-ly\nbizarre."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51600,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All these filters do is remove light – they\n“filter” it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55190,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you take a third filter, orient it\n45 degrees off from the first filter, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59960,
    "dDurationMs": 3369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put it between the two, the lamp will actually\nlook brighter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63329,
    "dDurationMs": 4991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is not the middle filter generating more\nlight – somehow introducing another filter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68320,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually lets more light through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70140,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With perfect filters, if you keep adding\nmore and more in between at in-between angles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74470,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this trend continues – more light!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76740,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  This feels super weird."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79220,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it’s not just weird that more light\ncomes through; when you dig in quantitatively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82860,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to exactly how much more comes through, the\nnumbers don’t just seem too high, they seem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87650,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "impossibly high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88910,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when we tug at this thread, it leads to\nan experiment a little more sophisticated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92620,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than this sunglasses demo that forces us to\nquestion some very basic assumptions we have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96630,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the way the universe works – like,\nthat the results of experiments describe properties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100330,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the thing you’re experimenting on, and\nthat cause and effect don’t travel faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103520,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104770,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant:  Where we're headed is Bell’s theorem:\none of the most thought-provoking discoveries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109660,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in modern physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110810,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To appreciate it, it’s worth understanding\na little of the math used to represent quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115370,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "states, like the polarization of a photon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117690,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We actually made a second video showing\nmore of the details for how this works, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121340,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can find on 3blue1brown, but for now let’s\njust hit the main points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125799,
    "dDurationMs": 5031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, photons are waves in a thing called\nthe electromagnetic field, and polarization"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130830,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just means the direction in which that wave\nis wiggling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133690,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134690,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Polarizing filters absorb this wiggling\nenergy in one direction, so the wave coming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138740,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out the other side is wiggling purely in the\ndirection perpendicular to the one where energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143920,
    "dDurationMs": 1289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absorption is happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145209,
    "dDurationMs": 5261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike a water or sound wave, photons\nare quantum objects, and as such they either"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150470,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pass through a polarizer completely, or not\nat all, and this is apparently probabilistic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155430,
    "dDurationMs": 3919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like how we don’t know whether or not Schrodinger’s\nCat will be alive or dead until we look in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159349,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the box."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160349,
    "dDurationMs": 3821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: For anyone uncomfortable with the nondeterminism\nof quantum mechanics, it’s tempting to imagine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164170,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that a probabilistic event like this might\nhave some deeper cause that we just don’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168090,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "know yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169090,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That there is some “hidden variable”\ndescribing the photon’s state that would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171950,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tell us with certainty whether it should pass\nthrough a given filter or not, and maybe that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176330,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "variable is just too subtle for us to probe\nwithout deeper theories and better measuring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "devices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180920,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or maybe it’s somehow fundamentally unknowable,\nbut still there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184690,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  The possibility of such a hidden\nvariable seems beyond the scope of experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189110,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, what measurements could possibly\nprobe at a deeper explanation that might or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193590,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might not exist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194730,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, we can do just that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196700,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant:...With sunglasses and polarization\nof light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199150,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Let’s lay down some numbers here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201200,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When light passes through a polarizing filter\noriented vertically, then comes to another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205400,
    "dDurationMs": 5350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polarizing filter oriented the same way, experiments\nshow that it’s essentially guaranteed to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210750,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make it through the second filter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If that second filter is tilted 90 degrees\nfrom the first, then each photon has a 0%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217560,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chance of passing through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219060,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at 45 degrees, there’s a 50/50 chance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222090,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: What’s more, these probabilities\nseem to only depend on the angle between the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225870,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two filters in question, and nothing else\nthat happened to the photon before, including"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229819,
    "dDurationMs": 2151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "potentially having passed through a different\nfilter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231970,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: But the real numerical weirdness happens\nwith filters oriented less than 45° apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236680,
    "dDurationMs": 7279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, at 22.5 degrees, any photon which\npasses through the first filter has an 85%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243959,
    "dDurationMs": 1731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chance of passing through the second filter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245690,
    "dDurationMs": 3269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see where all these numbers come from,\nby the way, check out the second video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248959,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249959,
    "dDurationMs": 3161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: What’s strange about that last number\nis that you might expect it to be more like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "halfway between 50% and 100% since 22.5°\nis halfway between 0° and 45° – but it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significantly higher."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260280,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: To see concretely how strange this\nis, let’s look at a particular arrangement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264160,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our three filters:  A, oriented vertically,\nB, oriented 22.5 degrees from vertical, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270060,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C, oriented 45 degrees from vertical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272020,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re going to compare just how many photons\nget blocked when B isn’t there with how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276280,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many get blocked when B is there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278190,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When B is not there, half of those passing\nthrough A get blocked at C.  That is, filter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283410,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C makes the lamp look half as bright as it\nwould with just filter A."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286650,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: But once you insert B, like we said,\n85% of those passing through A pass through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291610,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "B, which means 15% are blocked at B.  And\n15% of those that pass through B are blocked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297220,
    "dDurationMs": 5930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at C. But how on earth does blocking 15% twice\nadd up to the 50% blocked if B isn’t there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303150,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it doesn’t, which is why the lamp\nlooks brighter when you insert filter B, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307500,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it really makes you wonder how the universe\nis deciding which photons to let through and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311690,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which ones to block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: In fact, these numbers suggest that\nit’s impossible for there to be some hidden"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316840,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "variable determining each photon’s state\nwith respect to each filter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320690,
    "dDurationMs": 6390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, if each one has some definite answers\nto the three questions “Would it pass through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327080,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A”, “Would it pass through B” and “Would\nit pass through C”, even before those measurements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331400,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332400,
    "dDurationMs": 5359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: We’ll do a proof by contradiction,\nwhere we imagine 100 photons who do have some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337759,
    "dDurationMs": 4631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hidden variable which, through whatever crazy\nunderlying mechanism you might imagine, determines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342390,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their answers to these questions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343770,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And let’s say all of these will definitely\npass through A, which I’ll show by putting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348040,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all 100 inside this circle representing photons\nthat pass through A."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351990,
    "dDurationMs": 5032,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: To produce the results we see in experiments,\nabout 85 of these photons would have to have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357022,
    "dDurationMs": 4568,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a hidden variable determining that they pass\nthrough B, so let’s put 85 of these guys"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361590,
    "dDurationMs": 5730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the intersection of A and B, leaving 15\nin this crescent moon section representing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367320,
    "dDurationMs": 7400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photons that pass A but not B. Similarly,\namong those 85 that would pass through B,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374720,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 15% would get blocked by C, which is\nrepresented in this little section inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380500,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the A and B circles, but outside the C circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383560,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the actual number whose hidden variable\nhas them passing through both A and B but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388590,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not C is certainly no more than 15."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391860,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: But think of what Henry was just saying,\nwhat was weird was that when you remove filter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396510,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "B, never asking the photons what they think\nabout 22.5 degree angles, the number that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402080,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get blocked at C seems much too high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405310,
    "dDurationMs": 5109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So look back at our Venn diagram, what does\nit mean if a photon has some hidden variable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410419,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "determining that it passes A but is blocked\nat C?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414530,
    "dDurationMs": 5609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It means it’s somewhere in this crescent\nmoon region inside circle A and outside circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420139,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421139,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Now, experiments show that a full 50\nof these 100 photons that pass through A should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426759,
    "dDurationMs": 5891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get blocked at C, but if we take into account\nhow these photons would behave with B there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432650,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that seems impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434580,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Either those photons would have passed through\nB, meaning they’re somewhere in this region"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439580,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we talked about of passing both A and B but\ngetting blocked at C, which includes fewer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444680,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than 15 photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446540,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or they would have been blocked by B, which\nputs them in a subset of this other crescent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451300,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "moon region representing those passing A and\ngetting blocked at B, which has 15 photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457660,
    "dDurationMs": 6940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the number passing A and getting blocked\nat C should be strictly smaller than 15 +"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464600,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "15...but at the same time it’s supposed\nto be 50?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466979,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does that work?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468639,
    "dDurationMs": 4571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Remember, that number 50 is coming\nfrom the case where the photon is never measured"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473210,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at B, and all we’re doing is asking what\nwould have happened if it was measured at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478250,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "B, assuming that it has some definite state\neven when we don’t make the measurement,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484000,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that gives this numerical contradiction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: For comparison, think of any other,\nnon-quantum questions you might ask."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491080,
    "dDurationMs": 3941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, take a hundred people, and ask them\nif they like minutephysics, if they have a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495021,
    "dDurationMs": 2229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beard, and if they wear glasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497250,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, obviously everyone likes minutephysics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499430,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then among those, take the number that don’t\nhave beards, plus the number who do have a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504350,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beard but not glasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505900,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That should greater than or equal to the\nnumber who don’t have glasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509580,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, one is a superset of the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511860,
    "dDurationMs": 6169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as absurdly reasonable as that is, some\nquestions about quantum states seem to violate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518029,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this inequality, which contradicts the premise\nthat these questions could have definite answers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522919,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523919,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  Well...Unfortunately, there’s a\nhole in that argument."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527699,
    "dDurationMs": 4151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Drawing those Venn diagrams assumes that\nthe answer to each question is static and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531850,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unchanging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532850,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if the act of passing through one\nfilter changes how the photon will later interact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536160,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with other filters?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537230,
    "dDurationMs": 3229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you could easily explain the results\nof the experiment, so we haven’t proved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540459,
    "dDurationMs": 3331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hidden variable theories are impossible; just\nthat any hidden variable theory would have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543790,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to have the interaction of the particle with\none filter affect the interaction of the particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547920,
    "dDurationMs": 1089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with other filters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549009,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  We can, however, rig up an experiment\nwhere the interactions cannot affect each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552709,
    "dDurationMs": 4391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other without faster than light communication,\nbut where the same impossible numerical weirdness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557100,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "persists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558100,
    "dDurationMs": 3729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The key is to make photons pass not through\nfilters at different points in time, but at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561829,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different points in space at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564089,
    "dDurationMs": 1451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for this, you need entanglement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565540,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: For this video, what we'll mean when\nwe say two photons are \"entangled\" is that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569040,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you were to pass each one of them through\nfilters oriented the same way, either both"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572829,
    "dDurationMs": 1721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pass through, or both get blocked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574550,
    "dDurationMs": 3199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, they behave the same way when measured\nalong the same axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577749,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this correlated behavior persists no matter\nhow far away the photons and filters are from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582009,
    "dDurationMs": 3221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each other, even if there's no way for one\nphoton to influence the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585230,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unless, somehow, it did so faster than the\nspeed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587920,
    "dDurationMs": 1109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that would be crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589029,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant:  So now here’s what you do for the\nentangled version of our photon-filter experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593579,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of sending one photon through multiple\npolarizing filters, you’ll send entangled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598189,
    "dDurationMs": 5251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pairs of photons to two far away locations,\nand simultaneously at each location, randomly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603440,
    "dDurationMs": 3199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "choose one filter to put in the path of that\nphoton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606639,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doing this many times, you’ll collect a\nlot of data about how often both photons in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611010,
    "dDurationMs": 3329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an entangled pair pass through the different\ncombinations of filters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614339,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  But the thing is, you still see all\nthe same numbers as before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617589,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you use filter A at one site and filter\nB at the other, among all those that pass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622059,
    "dDurationMs": 4751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through filter A, about 15% have an entangled\npartner that gets blocked at B.  Likewise,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626810,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if they’re set to B and C, about 15% of\nthose that do pass through B have an entangled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631470,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "partner that gets blocked by C.  And with\nsettings A and C, half of those that through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635819,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A get blocked at C."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637239,
    "dDurationMs": 3611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: Again, if you think carefully about\nthese numbers, they seem to contradict the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640850,
    "dDurationMs": 3679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "idea that there can be some hidden variable\ndetermining the photon’s states."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644529,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, draw the same Venn Diagram as before,\nwhich assumes that each photon actually does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649709,
    "dDurationMs": 3701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have some definite answers to the questions\n“Would it pass through A”, “Would it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653410,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pass through B” and “Would it pass through\nC”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655610,
    "dDurationMs": 4479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: If, as Henry said, 15% of those that\npass through A get blocked at B, we should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660089,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nudge these circles a bit so that only 15%\nof the area of circle A is outside circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666059,
    "dDurationMs": 5950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "B.  Likewise, based on the data from entangled\npairs measured at B and C, only 15% of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672009,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photons which pass through B would get blocked\nat C, so this region here inside B and outside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677019,
    "dDurationMs": 2091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "C needs to be sufficiently small."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679110,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: But that really limits the number of\nphotons that would pass through A and get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683900,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blocked by C.  Why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685350,
    "dDurationMs": 6909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the region representing photons passing\nA and blocked at C is entirely contained inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692259,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the previous two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693259,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, what quantum mechanics predicts,\nand what these entanglement experiments verify,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697449,
    "dDurationMs": 5271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that a full 50% of those measured to pass\nthrough A should have an entangled partner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702720,
    "dDurationMs": 1309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "getting blocked at C."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704029,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: If you assume that all these circles\nhave the same size, which means any previously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708749,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unmeasured photon has no preference for one\nof these filters over the others, there is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712889,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "literally no way to accurately represent all\nthree of these proportions in a diagram like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717879,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this, so it’s not looking good for hidden\nvariable theories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721569,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry:  Again, for a hidden variable theory\nto survive, this can only be explained if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726069,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the photons are able to influence each other\nbased on which filters they passed through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729709,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now we have a much stronger result,\nbecause in the case of entangled photons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733959,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this influence would have to be faster than\nlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736359,
    "dDurationMs": 3861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: The assumption that there is some deeper\nunderlying state to a particle even if it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740220,
    "dDurationMs": 2239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not being probed is called “realism”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742459,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the assumption that faster than light\ninfluence is not possible is called “locality”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747220,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What this experiment shows is that either\nrealism is not how the universe works, or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752480,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "locality is not how the universe works, or\nsome combination (whatever that means)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757060,
    "dDurationMs": 3689,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: Specifically, it’s not that quantum\nentanglement appears to violate realism or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760749,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the speed of light while actually being locally\nreal at some underlying level - it the contradictions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765089,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this experiment show it CANNOT be locally\nreal, period."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768179,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: What we’ve described here is one\nexample of what's called a Bell inequality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772290,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a simple counting relationship that\nmust be obeyed by a set of questions with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777170,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "definite answers, but which quantum states\nseem to disobey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780170,
    "dDurationMs": 4399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: In fact, the mathematics of quantum\ntheory predicts that entangled quantum states"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784569,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should violate Bell inequalities in exactly\nthis way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787769,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "John Bell originally put out the inequalities\nand the observation that quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791959,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would violate them in 1964."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793709,
    "dDurationMs": 4081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: Since then, numerous experiments have\nput it into practice, but it turns out it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797790,
    "dDurationMs": 3479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite difficult to get all your entangled\nparticles and detectors to behave just right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801269,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which can mean observed violations of this\ninequality might end with certain “loopholes”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804959,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that might leave room for locality and realism\nto both be true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808369,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first loophole-free test happened only\nin 2015."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811359,
    "dDurationMs": 4371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grant: There have also been numerous theoretical\ndevelopments in the intervening years, strengthening"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815730,
    "dDurationMs": 4959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bell’s and other similar results (that is,\nstrengthening the case against local realism)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820689,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Henry: In the end, here’s what I find crazy:\nBell’s Theorem is an incredibly deep result"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825299,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upending what we know about how our universe\nworks that humanity has only just recently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828879,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come to know, and yet the math at its heart\nis a simple counting argument, and the underlying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832939,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physical principles can be seen in action\nwith a cheap home demo!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836209,
    "dDurationMs": 4791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s frankly surprising more people don’t know about it"
    } ]
  } ]
}
